{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/1564074-splat-based-created","id":1564074,"title":"Splat Based Created","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Promethean: The Created"],"posts":[{"date":"2026-09-15T01:46:54-07:00","id":1564074,"title":"Splat Based Created","content":"I'm running a thought experiment that may or may not evolve into a chronicle. The goal isn't necessarily to build a single cohesive scenario, but a series of independent ones.<br /> <br /> Each puts a supernatural splat in an otherwise &quot;regular&quot; genesis situation of their kind, but the process goes wrong. And it would have just failed were it not for the Azoth.<br /> <br /> Then it splits: how could both mechanically and narratively be an Extempore born out of this? And how would it be if instead it was an actual new Lineage? <hr /><br /> VAMPIRE<br /> <br /> The Undead tried the Embrace. Exanguinate your target, feed them your Vitae, invest some of yourself in the process to will the Curse into taking hold.<br /> <br /> Sometimes it goes wrong for any of numerous reasons. The body didn't raise at first. It was a failure. But being Vitae doesn't impede the red liquid within a vampire from being a Humour, and the Divine Fire made itself present.<br /> <br /> For the Progenitor version, the vampire may have been really desperate to see it succeed, and tried something with their own blood that fed the Alchemy. <hr /><br /> WEREWOLF<br /> <br /> A Pack had been following a soon to be Uratha for a time, now. They really wanted them in the group, maybe even they already are, just didn't undergone the First Transformation yet.<br /> <br /> But things turn ugly when the time is come. The boy end up severely mauled and is in their last breath while an Ithaeur tries to heal them with whatever scraps of Essence they can manage. It is, indeed, too late, even if the body is still in Gauru form.<br /> <br /> It was still in Gauru when the Divine Fire infused it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-09-15T11:48:12-07:00","id":1564090,"title":"","content":"For inspiration, I'd suggest taking a look at 1e's Saturnine Night, specifically the &quot;Impossibilities&quot; section on pp. 32-39, which outlines what Created with a vampire, werewolf, or mage demiurge might look like.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/51-marin","name":"marin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2019"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-09-15T16:49:01-07:00","id":1564101,"title":"","content":"I've been toying with the idea of a tentative Fetch turning up as a Promethean. The Fae craft the wannabe imposter, maybe within a firestorm, and the Azoth do the trick, creating an Extempore.<br /> <br /> Or maybe they actually learned some Alchemy and thought it would be a nice addition to their experiments. Such a Fae could even be behind an upsurge in the formation of Created with the Lineage they just started.<br /> <br /> A Conspiracy could create a Promethean in an accident that failed to cause Divergence, or find one method of Creation thinking it is like a new Divergence or something.<br /> <br /> What if a Hero and a Horror kill each other and are both transformed? For the Divine Fire is the nature of their composition an impediment at all?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-09-15T17:38:19-07:00","id":1564104,"title":"","content":"Data point: the Seven Wonders of the World Dark Era involves Prometheans and Changelings in a setting where Azoth has been contaminates with Glamour (or is it the other way around?) and in this setting, it's possible for Fetches to choose to take on the Pilgrimage. The fact that some of them very nearly achieved the New Dawn is what moved the Gentry to being about the end of this state of affairs. <br /> <br /> For personal reasons (I have a trio of personal \u201ciconic characters\u201d for Changeling: a Changeling, her elderly Fetch, and her same-age Fae-Touched daughter), I'm very much interested in ideas that would allow a Fetch to embark on the Pilgrimage in modern times, <i>without </i>the Seven Wonders of the World making it possible. <br /> <br /> I suspect that every other example of Splat-based Created will require the would-be new member of the splat dying during the attempted conversion; but instead of staying dead, the Divine Fire takes over and animates them as an Extempore based on what they would have become. <br /> <br /> For the would-be Uratha, give them a Bestowment adapted from WtF2e's Wolf-blooded Tells. Note that those Tells include, among other things limited lycanthropy; so if you want your Werewolf-Created to actually be a werewolf, go with one of those Tells. <br /> <br /> For a would-be Awakened, the result ought to be somewhat along the lines of a Harrowed Banisher, save only for the fact that the result <i>isn't </i>a mage; he just simulates being a mage through his alchemy. Prometheans might even confuse him for an Alchemist. <br /> <br /> Hunter is largely immune to this sort of thing; those cases where a third-tier Conspiracy attempts to make major modifications to an agent and it goes terribly wrong are arguably better addressed as a Deviant Divergence gone horribly wrong. <br /> <br /> Geist has the \u201cthe host has to die first\u201d things already built in; all you need is for the joining with the Geist to go horribly wrong. I picture this Extempore as vaguely resembling the Ulgans, but ghost-themed instead of spirit-themed. <br /> <br /> Mummy and Demon share the problem that their protagonists were never technically human. <br /> <br /> Beast isn't my cup of tea, so I can't offer much on it. <br /> <br /> Deviant features humans being experimented on, which could easily lead to the humans dying.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-09-15T20:16:02-07:00","id":1564110,"title":"","content":"Oh, death is a given. You don't turn into a Created, you're born one from the materials offered. If the witnesses notice it or not is besides the point.<br /> <br /> The idea of using their transformation process is to distance the Creation from usual lineages. If you use the methods to create a Thamuz in a Werewolf corpse, lingering effects or not, the result &quot;should&quot; be a Thamuz.<br /> <br /> Here the process is either creating Extempore with the thematic background/lingering energy possibly guiding the result, or it is modified to an actual Creation, engendering a new Lineage. That I let for whomever wants to use it to decide, I may try both.<br /> <br /> Of course as normal a Lineage has a Demiurge, so in this case the participant will be following all the requisites even if unaware that their new method will make something else. The catch is that an unusual but plausible deviation of their regular transformation points is frequently indistinguishable from the situations that beget a Promethean.<br /> <br /> I wasn't thinking on making Hunter because of precisely what you said, though it may be that this attempt to turn one into a superior hunter ends up in death and Creation, but then that'd be less interesting for this exercise.<br /> <br /> Geist, Demon and Beast don't offer a problem, but actually an interesting twist: the material itself. Prometheans are more easily Made from human remains or human likeness, but if they can also be made of cans, marble, machines and CPUs, what happens when they're Made of whatever those creatures are composed of?<br /> <br /> Geist may give us an Ulgan like or even a Geist genuinely tied to a would-be Human, but as an alternative take we can have a Promethean built of debris from the Underworld, Memories from the Ocean, maybe even a Ghost struck by a Pyros lightning is destroyed and the Corpus reborn as a Created. The ghost may or may not Reform elsewhere after this madness.<br /> <br /> Demons have a body made of whatever it is the God-Machine uses for construction, altered in whatever fashion the Fall alters them. Being struck right of the moment of the Fall would be a way to have a Promethean made of an Angel at the point of disconnect with the God-Machine. Later it can be done with the corpse of a Demon proper, earlier it will just involve a lot more of God-Machine attention. In all cases Covers may play a role in the result or not, as a state that's at least thematically similar to a Role.<br /> <br /> Beast has two previous entities, a Human and a Horror. The Human has their soul devoured, being another Splat with something alien in its place. What happens if the Horror devours the newly formed Azoth-soul instead? And Beast makes it possible for the Horror, a denizen of the Astral in the frontier between the Temenos and the Anima Mundi, to materialize without changing form. That's usually not the case, but it can, and that means for an instant at least a path exists for Pyros to touch Astral matter in a Creation. A Hero turned Demiurge could also bring Pyros to the Lair of a Beast and do their gruesome job led by the same mania that is so common among Demiurges, is tainted by the narcissistic tendencies of a Hero.<br /> <br /> Finally, you're forgetting something: Mummies were human. I don't think using the corpse of a Mummy would fit the exercise, although killing a Sekhem 10 monster and capturing this power within the Progenitor would be rad as Hell. But what would have happened back in Irem if one or a few of the Arisen died in the ritual, but something still reanimated the bodies? In fact it has the advantage that the scope of the ritual allows for multiple independent Creation events across the country, be it Extempore or a minor priest, worker, rogue Shan'Iatu, even intervention of the Judges. A Created that exists in a form, or maybe even the full form, of Timelessness.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-09-16T02:25:38-07:00","id":1564117,"title":"","content":"A few extra data points:<br /> <i>&quot;Night Horrors: The Tormented</i>&quot; has a Pandoran created from a Uratha's corpse. Their semi-spiritual nature did affect the result, though I can't offer details without the book on me.<br /> <i>&quot;Dark Eras 2 (French Revolution)&quot;</i> shows that Mummies can be Embraced while in Henet (Torpor analogue), creating a mindless abomination. That's a solvable problem for Arisen characters, since once they return from Duat, the can just recreate new bodies via their Talisman, Canopic Jars, or outright taking over an Inheritor's body. The precedent shows that other occult powers (like Azoth) can successfully meddle with an inert body like that.<br /> <br /> I remember being inspired by how <i>&quot;Seven Wonders of the Ancient World&quot;</i> enabled Fetches to begin a Pilgrimage. It made me think how the only theoretical requirement for beginning the Pilgrimage could just be not having been human before. That would mean that with the proper transference of Azoth, you could &quot;uplift&quot; Strix, Spirits, Shartha, Ghosts (if they internalize they're a new person), Hobgoblins, Unchained, Unchained Covers turned independent, Angels, Horrors and mundane living animals.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>~<span style=\"color:#222222\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\">\u266b</span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7593-teatime","name":"Teatime","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7593_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"750"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-09-16T10:07:52-07:00","id":1564123,"title":"","content":"Uplifting with Azoth has a few extra challenges in canon.<br /> <br /> First, it's damn volatile. Most things hit by it don't come the other side just slightly modified or carrying a proto-soul, they get mutated and dead. Mostly dead.<br /> <br /> Also when it does affect someone in a subtler, non explosive way, the result is a Demiurge: the being won't gain a soul, but seek to Create. And this has no requirement of being Human.<br /> <br /> Now, I can think of someone weird exceptions happening, especially when it comes to Azoth, but the remaining question is what it would even mean to them.<br /> <br /> Such entities are all naturally occurring in their environments, and have already a source of Drive and fulfillment. They're not Human, but they're not meant to be, either. A Promethean is an artificial construct animated to be a person, their origin is an act of artificial generation by definition, in a world not meant for them and in an ongoing process of transmutation, the act is not finished.<br /> <br /> I can see a lot of ways this can resonate with a Fetch, but the others? What does it mean to them? What becoming Human entails? And are the themes and mechanics of Promethean the best way to handle it?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-09-16T11:54:17-07:00","id":1564125,"title":"","content":"Part of the challenge here, of course, is that Promethean is a weird-exception-heavy game to such a degree that the Extempore in 2e are the designated folder for particularly unique exceptions, and most of the comparable published cross-splat creations are related to (or at least adjacent to) the Contagion due to easy justification.<br /> <br /> Deviant and Mage's metaphysical basis in the soul and its foundations (and Mummy's to a lesser extent) can explain a lot of different aberrations in the natural order from their neck of the woods without necessarily resembling an existing phenomenon, but the specific volatility of Azoth makes it tricky to focus down into splat-based phenomena without getting more specific for the needs of a given game or storyhook, especially for splats with broader basic concepts than Vampire and Werewolf.<br /> <br /> The &quot;not all gamelines' monsters are suited to this premise&quot; aspect of the discussion does bring in the premise of Dyads and other secondary monster types from the games as consideration.<br /> <br /> For instance, demons don't create other demons except in the sense that any conversant being could potentially precipitate a Fall, but they can definitely create stigmatics, activate demon-blooded, or sire/birth Fractals, any one of which could be inadvertently used as raw materials for a Promethean in an Aetheric mishap (which could also be triggered by Infrastructural error or as the deliberate or unintended product of an especially intricate occult matrix). Calling in a soul pact also has the potential to go awry for mysterious reasons that may have nothing to do with the displacement of a whole individual soul from the world, but since the Cover such an act normally creates is a product of durable faith in an active deception of the world it becomes difficult to come up with how such a thing shapes the resulting Created besides the corebook precedent of Anthony as an Extempore who is the dream of a child for someone to fill a role.<br /> <br /> In the opposite direction, new mummies may not be created anymore, but their Inheritors take a bit of their soul into themselves and being integrated into their master's soul is a turbulent process that takes a whole Descent to complete; divine power may not sit right for everyone in the installation or the override. In the other direction, just because the Rite of Return is theoretically impossible to actually repeat in the worldstate following its completion, nothing stops someone from trying to do so anyway \u2014 unless they're intentionally or unintentionally downscaling the process, it would probably take a particular sort of drive to involve a large number of candidate bodies-to-be, and it's hard not to compare the typical failure rate and body count of most Divergence methodologies from Deviant for the sort of operation such a thing would suggest.<br /> <br /> I would frankly go the opposite direction from prior suggestions for Geist: a Created being emerging from a failed Bargain doesn't result in a Promethean with a geist Bound to them, it results in a pseudo-Orphean Created with a Deathmask stuck to their face, false life born from the doubly dead, with River water pouring through its veins.<br /> <br /> Returning to the well of peripheral phenomena, Beasts don't even need to start at the moment of the Devouring to provide side roads to Creation \u2014 any Begotten can create Horrorspawn and try to give them a body (either already dead or soon to be killed by the process), and this process in turn is compared to the Rampant Inheritance where a Beast's Horror breaks containment to warp their body in a way whose peripheral side-effect of subtly warping the landscape around the resulting creature isn't difficult to compare to a Wasteland.<br /> <br /> Mage has the established precedent of Supernal beings consuming and wearing the guise of those who enter the Supernal Realms without the protection of a Lustrum, and there's an entire category of (comparatively rare) metamorphic Awakening whose effect is just &quot;a weird Mystery or strange place is added to the setting because of this,&quot; to say nothing of the Nimbus as a phenomenon \u2014 mages come back from the dead as a result of their Awakenings fairly often, and far less often they come back with their souls cracked open and their sympathetic names erased, so bad luck on the breaking point that kicks off the Adyton (or a chance encounter with a Firestorm while the Prospect is undergoing the trials) could produce something that superficially resembles a mage whose Awakening wiped out all their memories, poisoned their Nimbus, and left them with a number of stable magical powers without the Enraptured degree of obsession.<br /> <br /> Deviant can hit similar notes through what Shallow Graves introduces as the &quot;extinction burst&quot; effect of the End Stage, guaranteeing the death of the Remade who triggered it in exchange for some awful or miraculous event, including Divergence events, various anomalies, or permanent occult scars on the world, and even without such an extra dramatic layer the failure result of a deviant's soul burning out is not necessarily biological death and may instead be the loss of their mind or their transformation into something that cannot have meaningful human interactions, either of which is prime narrative real estate for putting their remains to a different use.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-09-16T20:18:33-07:00","id":1564134,"title":"","content":"As you say, Promethean is a game about exceptions; and for the most part, the Extempore are the extremes of that. But I might go a different route for a Promethean based on the Unchained: typically, an Unchained develops a Cover when it Falls; and any Unchained who fails to do so doesn't last long. But consider the possibility of an Angel of the God-Machine Falling during a Firestorm, or during a conflict with a <i>qashmal</i>. The angel decides that it doesn't just want to side with humanity against the God-Machine; it decides that it wants to <i>become human. </i>And for whatever bizarre reason, the Principle honors the wish. Instead of developing a Cover, the former Angel becomes an Unfleshed Promethean with the usual Azothic disguise hiding its Disfigurements, kind of like how a Cover normally conceals the Unchained.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}